From b1e86d889cce27ea016e2859a67cab39bfd9a48f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amandeep Singh <amanr268@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:53:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] mfd: core: give children of non-DMA parents a dma_mask
 pointer

An MFD child of an I2C device inherits a NULL dma_mask. When the child
has a DT node, of_dma_configure() then warns "DMA mask not set" (seen
for tps65217-pwrbutton) and points dma_mask at coherent_dma_mask.
Set that pointer when the device is created, so the end result is the
same without the warning.
---
 drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c b/drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c
index 256058a6e..58b10f585 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c
@@ -187,6 +187,13 @@ static int mfd_add_device(struct device *parent, int id,
 	pdev->dev.dma_mask = parent->dma_mask;
 	pdev->dev.dma_parms = parent->dma_parms;
 	pdev->dev.coherent_dma_mask = parent->coherent_dma_mask;
+	/*
+	 * Children of non-DMA parents (I2C/SPI PMICs) have no dma_mask;
+	 * of_dma_configure() would set it to the coherent mask anyway, but
+	 * only after warning "DMA mask not set". Do it here, quietly.
+	 */
+	if (!pdev->dev.dma_mask)
+		pdev->dev.dma_mask = &pdev->dev.coherent_dma_mask;
 
 	ret = regulator_bulk_register_supply_alias(
 			&pdev->dev, cell->parent_supplies,
